From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 13:19:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00485/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for FR-11 continuous
 self-learning v21 (the mandated self-learning experiment) -- does the Tier-3
 fast-path operating point GENERALIZE? v20 (exp3803) wired the trained
 predictor as a fast-path/early-exit gate and measured skip 0.56 / effective
 AUROC 0.9227 in the frozen CI on ONE held-out split. v21 re-measures the SAME
 persisted operating point on a SECOND held-out seed/split (disjoint from both
 the predictor's training split AND the v20 measurement split) to confirm the
 skip-rate + no-regression hold out-of-sample -- or report HONESTLY that the
 operating point is split-specific and needs recalibration. Reuses the
 persisted predictor; runs NO live model; the frozen 0.9131 full-scoring
 ensemble stays the fall-through (untouched).

Co-Authored-By: Gemini CLI <noreply@google.com>
